-- title:
--   Pauli Soundness
-- statement:
--   There exist universal real constants $a,b$ with $1\le a$ and $0<b<1$ such that, for every Pauli parameter package $P$, error $\varepsilon\ge0$, and strategy $S$ with value at least $1-\varepsilon$, one can extract a Pauli-register witness $w$. Its state error and every raw Alice and Bob Pauli error obey
--
--   $$\operatorname{error}\le\delta_{\mathrm{QLD}}(a,b,\varepsilon;P.m,P.d,P.q).$$
--
--   $P$ determines the compact game and fixed field model, $S$ is the original strategy, and $w$ is the extracted representation. This is the qudit Pauli-basis soundness theorem.
--
